# @podlite/toc

=head1 Upcoming

=item B<Breaking:> a C<:caption> written on a table of contents is shown as text, markup codes and all, so a C<G<>> in it no longer hides anything; a caption C<=set> gives keeps its codes. The entry of a block whose caption C<=set> gives hides what the caption hides

=head1 0.0.70

=item B<Breaking:> a table of contents takes its caption from C<:caption> only; C<:title> is no longer read, and an entry for a table of contents that another one lists is not named by its C<:title> either, in C<getContentForToc> as well. A folded table of contents without a caption shows C<Contents> in C<@podlite/to-jsx>. Blocks other than a table of contents still name their entry by C<:title>

=head1 0.0.69

=item C<:title> as the caption of a table of contents is deprecated: it is still read in this release and will not be in the next. The specification captions a table of contents with C<:caption>, and C<podlite lint> warns about C<:title> (rule C<toc-title-attribute>)

=item an entry for a heading leads to that heading, not to the first heading with the same text: two C<=head1 Intro> get entries to C<#Intro> and C<#Intro-2>, and so do a heading of the page and one of an included file. The entry carries the heading's key instead of its text, so the address of an entry for a heading with hidden text holds none of it. A heading named with C<:id>, written or set, keeps that name

=head1 0.0.64

=item C<rebuildToc> builds the table a C<=toc> block holds again over a tree that gained blocks, such as those an include brought, reading the selector from the table and the configuration from the block; a table that keeps no selector is left as it is

=item the first non-blank line of C<=toc> is read as a selector: predicates and C<*> apply, and the lines after it are not read. Patterns are separated by commas. A selector that cannot be read, holds a markup code, names a source or needs a file makes a table without entries and a warning. The table does not list itself, and with C<*> it does not list comments, data or includes it does not name

=item a paragraph or code written without a marker is titled by its text, and a block whose name has no lowercase letter stands as a first-level heading; such a block used to stop the whole document from being built

=item C<=toc> and C<=Toc> stay blocks of the name they were written with, with their configuration and place, and hold the table of contents they make in their content. A selection finds them, C<*> among it, and a block already holding its table is not made again when the tree is built twice

=item the caption of a table of contents is parsed the way a picture caption is: its markup codes become nodes of the new C<caption> field, and a hidden word in it is marked as hidden. C<title> keeps the caption as written

=item an entry of a table of contents hides what its source hides: the text of a hidden heading, picture or table caption, a hidden word inside a heading, and every entry of a hidden table of contents. Open words stay open, and a link, note, alias or definition inside a heading comes into the entry as its text

=head1 0.0.63

=item the package can be imported from Node directly. The emitted ESM referenced its own files without an extension, which the ESM loader refuses


=head1 0.0.41

=item add C<exports> map, top-level C<types>, and explicit C<sideEffects> to package manifest

=head1 0.0.31

=item added C<:folded-levels{k=>v}> key-value syntax — each level can now be marked folded (C<1>) or not (C<0>) independently, e.g. C<{2=>1, 3=>0}>. Array syntax C<[2,3]> still works as before
=item added bare C<:folded> attribute on C<=toc> — wraps the entire TOC in a collapsible C<<details>>. Accepts C<:!folded>/C<:folded(0)> for a disclosure that opens by default

=head1 0.0.28

=item added C<:folded-levels> attribute for C<=toc> block -- controls which TOC levels are collapsed by default (array syntax)

=head1 0.0.19

=item improved toc usage in the editor
=item added default logic to retrieve the text for the toc element

=head1 0.0.12

=item implement `:caption`

=head1 0.0.11

=item fix linking toc items

=head1 0.0.7

=item `=toc` now is standard block

=head1 0.0.6

=item refactor

=head1 0.0.5

=item update deps

=head1 0.0.4

=item update deps

=head1 0.0.3

=item adjust plugin API

=head1 0.0.2

=item update deps

=head1 0.0.1

=item initial release
=item implement Table of conents =Toc block
=item add support :caption for =table
